# RELEASE_MODEL — the deploy-from-main tripwire state (goal 35).
#
# This file is a TECHNICAL GATE, not prose. `scripts/release_model_gate.py`
# (run by scripts/check.sh, so pre-commit + Stop hook + CI all enforce it)
# reads the DECISION below and FAILS the build if any GitHub Actions workflow
# would AUTOMATICALLY deploy as a consequence of code reaching `main` while the
# decision is still "open".
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
#   CLAUDE.md's auto-merge autonomy is valid ONLY while nothing deploys from
#   `main` (blast radius = the repo, every merge a revertible squash). The
#   moment a real gateway serves traffic off `main`, auto-merge must stop —
#   otherwise an unattended run could squash-merge itself straight into a live
#   deploy. That tripwire used to live only as prose in CLAUDE.md; a prose rule
#   is not a control (2026-07-23 go-real premortem). This marker + gate make it
#   a control: an unattended run physically cannot go green while a
#   deploy-from-main workflow exists and the release model is undecided.
#
# DECISION values:
#   open     — the release model is NOT yet decided (needs-a-human, see GOALS.md
#              "Release model BEFORE anything deploys from main"). While open, no
#              workflow may auto-deploy from main. THIS IS THE SAFE DEFAULT.
#   decided  — a human has chosen the release model (manual promotion / release
#              branch / tagged deploy) and recorded it. Only then may a
#              deploy-from-main workflow land green.
#
# TO CLOSE THE DECISION (a human act — do NOT let an unattended run flip this):
#   1. decide the release model with a human and record it in docs + the PR body,
#   2. set DECISION=decided below,
#   3. and STOP auto-merging from CLAUDE.md's contract the moment main deploys.
#
# Scope: the gate fires on AUTOMATIC deploy-on-push-to-main (the trigger that
# kills auto-merge). Manual (workflow_dispatch) / tag / release deploys are a
# human pulling the trigger and are intentionally out of the AUTOMATIC tripwire
# — but they are themselves a release model, so per CLAUDE.md they still require
# this decision to be closed by a human first.
DECISION=open
